  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Kia Sportage?",
      "a": "Yes, with a DIMO device. The Telemetry API serves the fuel level signals, and the segments query with the refuel mechanism detects where fuel level rises significantly."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Kia Sportage with no connected services?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device, either the DIMO LTE R1 or AutoPi. Once the owner shares the vehicle with you, exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API and query the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I get check-engine light alerts for a Kia Sportage?",
      "a": "Yes, with the AutoPi DIMO device, which lists the dtc event and a diagnostic trouble code list signal. Push alerts to your server by creating a webhook in the Vehicle Triggers API and subscribing the vehicle to it."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Kia Sportage?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device and query segments with the idling mechanism. Idling segments are contiguous periods where engine RPM stays in the idle range, and the maxIdleRpm setting defaults to 1000."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Kia Sportage mileage?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device, which reports the odometer signal. To get a verifiable record, call the Attestation API odometer statement endpoint for the vehicle, then retrieve the result through the Telemetry API."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. For the Kia Sportage, an ICE vehicle, that data comes from a DIMO device on 2013 and newer model years, and this coverage has been tested. You read it through the Telemetry API, a GraphQL API, using a Vehicle JWT for each vehicle the owner has shared with you. The record lists the region as Global."
